# Persisted file/path values are repository-relative. Runtime checkout paths
# belong in the agent input only and must not be copied into this record.

<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-INGRESS-ADMIT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-INGRESS-ADMIT-001" ;
  triage:title "Local HTTP ingress on the replacement runtime fails admission under the official send benchmark: uds, tcp and tcp-tls lanes fail at f1 to f16 on 1.4.10 (accepted 1 of 1000, 95 rows persisted, connection closed before response headers); tcp on 1.4.9 admitted 600 of 1000 with HTTP 503 receiver-endpoint lookup failures" ;
  triage:description "Release-readiness step 1 on rand-m5/atmbench. Candidate 1.4.10 @ eefa01418 (campaign 20260903T185218Z-m5-atmbench, PR #1147): the sqlite lane PASSes (p50 43893.46 msg/s) but the first network lane, direct-v4 UDS f8 (raw trace 20260903-185252.408800-m5-atmbench-uds-f8.json on atmbench), records metrics requested_count=1000, accepted_count=1, durability_after_restart observed_mailbox_count=95 with expected_accepted_count=1 and durability passed=false; the first failure is that the daemon closed the local HTTP connection before response headers. The per-target diagnostic sweep on the same build shows UDS f1/f2/f4/f8 FAIL and f16/f64 PASS, TCP f1..f16 FAIL and f64 PASS, TCP-TLS f1..f16 FAIL and f64 PASS, each reported only as FAIL admission-capacity evidence with no reason text. Candidate 1.4.9 @ 2e3c93a7c (campaign 20260903T183628Z, PR #1146) already showed the tcp lane at p50 422.18 msg/s with messages_admitted=600 of 1000 and first_failure HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED failed to look up graft receiver endpoint (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/graft_receiver_endpoint_store.rs:211); uds and tcp-tls could not run on 1.4.9 because of RRG-BENCH-FQDN-001. Classification: product, blocking, against the replacement runtime local ingress (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs canonical write path around line 886, where local writes still await emit_received_hook before responding) and the graft receiver endpoint lookup that the hook performs; NOT the frozen legacy synchronous daemon. The mailbox holding 95 rows while only 1 admission was acknowledged means writes are persisted and then the response is lost or the connection is dropped, so the admission accounting seen by the client disagrees with durable state. Whether a1d4783c7 (peer-ingress hook detachment) changed local-path behaviour must be checked by rerunning uds f8 at 50e8614f9 versus a1d4783c7; the 1.4.9 tcp 503 evidence predates that commit, so the endpoint-lookup failure is at least partly pre-existing. Fix must land in atm-http-runtime or its storage adapters and be proven by a focused uds/tcp f8 rerun on atmbench before the full campaign. Fix round 3 (c1e521aa4: bounded idle pool for SharedDb control-path connections, bounded-backoff accept recovery) partially resolved it: focused uds f8 rerun on atmbench at c7f0fe7ec (2026-09-04T02:48Z, raw trace 20260904-024853.637104-local-uds-f8.json on atmbench) shows accepted_count equals durable rows equals 639 of 1000, so the closed-before-response-headers symptom and the accounting disagreement are gone, but 361 requests still received HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED during graft receiver endpoint lookup. Record stays open; residual mechanism (busy handling on control-path connections, effective concurrency bound, or the daemon RLIMIT_NOFILE soft limit under launchd) under root-cause on the same branch. Focused tcp f8 on the same commit (2026-09-04T02:49Z) also failed: accepted equals durable equals 662 of 1000, 338 HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED, first failure reported as failed to open SQLite database, which points at connection-open exhaustion under load rather than lock contention alone. Fix round 4 pushed as 9ed5b7dd1 (2026-09-04T03:2xZ): root cause is that ControlPathConnections bounded idle rather than live SQLite connections, so descriptor demand scaled with in-flight admissions and hit SQLITE_CANTOPEN extended code 14 (unable to open database file) under the launchd 256-fd soft limit; the endpoint-lookup message is the same code raised lazily at first read on the wal and shm sidecars, the tcp open-failure message is the same code at Connection open. Fix: new control_path_pool bounds live control-path connections at 8 with a Condvar wait bounded by the busy timeout and a RAII lease, plus descriptor_limit raise at HttpRuntime start as defence in depth. Local proof under ulimit -n 256: pre-fix 48 failures at concurrency 128 and 3034 at 160; post-fix 0 failures up to concurrency 256 with 38 to 42 fds peak. Regression tests in control_path_pool and descriptor_limit; just lint and just test exit 0. Awaiting focused uds and tcp f8 rerun on atmbench. Live proof on 9ed5b7dd1 (atmbench, 2026-09-04T03:14Z to 03:15Z, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 BENCH GO): focused uds f8 PASS, requested equals accepted equals durable equals 116000, no first failure, evidence 20260904-031403.388389-local-uds-f8.json; focused tcp f8 PASS, requested equals accepted equals durable equals 108000, no first failure, evidence 20260904-031452.110312-local-tcp-f8.json. Full step 1 (smoke, benchmark-official, benchmark-read) and the evidence PR follow under a separate BENCH GO. Closure verdict is quality-mgr's. Re-scope at QA-4c (arch-qa ARCH-002, 2026-09-04): occurrence CAND-1 (local-ingress writes await emit_received_hook inline before responding) is a distinct mechanism untouched by fix rounds 3 and 4 and is now tracked by RRG-INGRESS-LOCAL-HOOK-AWAIT-001 (important); this record covers only the descriptor-exhaustion mechanism (CAND-2, CAND-3) and its closure does not claim CAND-1. Full step 1 official benchmark at f5de13551 (campaign 20260904T033320Z-m5-atmbench, 2026-09-04T03:33Z to 03:4xZ, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 GO): admission is now correct on every lane (sqlite 924000 of 924000, uds 117000 of 117000, tcp 108000 of 108000, tcp-tls 145000 of 145000) but throughput FAILS the floors on all three network lanes: sqlite p50 48238.36 PASS; uds p50 6105.66 vs floor 18000; tcp p50 5523.52 vs floor 17000; tcp-tls p50 7371.04 vs floor 13500. Fix round 4 traded admission failures for a roughly three-fold throughput regression, so the record stays open and blocking; fix round 5 on the same branch must recover the floors without regressing admission (rule: no fix may regress numbers already hit). Prime suspect is the fix round 4 control_path_pool bound of 8 live connections with Condvar waiting on the blocking pool serialising endpoint lookups and the inline local received-hook await (RRG-INGRESS-LOCAL-HOOK-AWAIT-001) sitting inside that critical path; root cause to be established, not assumed. Evidence commit 257b39112 retained on atmbench; automatic push failed because the evidence branch name differs from the requested chore branch, evidence PR to follow. Occurrence CAND-4 records the regression at f5de13551. QA-4c/5 update 2026-09-04T03:41Z (quality-mgr): evidence PR for the FAIL campaign 20260904T033320Z at f5de13551 is https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1149 (develop base, same shape as #1147), recorded against occurrence CAND-4. Closure still waits on the fix-round-5 rerun evidence; QA-5 will run once arch-ctm pushes r5. Fix round 5 (3a9aa54d5: MAX_CONTROL_PATH_CONNECTIONS raised from 8 to 64 plus a 64-borrow regression test) DISPROVEN live: focused runs on atmbench at 3a9aa54d5 (2026-09-04T03:53Z to 03:54Z, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 focused GO) keep admission exact but drop throughput further: uds f8 p50 951.29 with accepted equal to durable equal to 18000 (evidence 20260904-035352.614851-local-uds-f8.json), tcp f8 p50 867.15 with 19000 (evidence 20260904-035431.426670-local-tcp-f8.json), no first failure. The r4 focused runs at 9ed5b7dd1 moved about 116000 messages in the same duration-bounded window, consistent with the official 6105 per second, so the wider bound made the control path roughly six times slower, which points at SQLite lock or busy-handler contention between control-path connections rather than a descriptor or queueing limit. The pool bound is therefore not the root cause of the gap to the floors; the floors (uds 18000, tcp 17000, tcp-tls 13500) were set on the AO2 replacement-runtime baseline before the graft receiver endpoint lookup and received-hook work landed on develop, and no network lane on this candidate has ever met them, so the regression window is the AO2 baseline to this branch, not only the candidate commits. Fix round 6 must root-cause by measurement (bisect on atmbench focused uds f8, including the AO2 baseline commit and the candidate merge-base with develop) before any further code change, and must not ship 3a9aa54d5 as is because it regresses the r4 number. Amendment v10 (2026-09-04T04:0xZ, team-lead ruling relayed via fenix@rand-m5): the r5 verdict above is downgraded from disproven to INCONCLUSIVE because the r5 focused runs were short (18000 and 19000 requests) versus the f5de13551 baseline (117000 and 108000) and cold-start or warmup skew cannot be excluded. A matched-length rerun at 3a9aa54d5 (about 100000 sustained per lane, uds f8 then tcp f8) is in progress on atmbench under a focused GO from fenix@rand-m5; its result decides r5. If it meets the floors, 3a9aa54d5 stands and the r6 bisect is cancelled; if it does not, the r6 measurement-first bisect proceeds and 3a9aa54d5 is superseded. No further code change lands before that result. Matched-length r5 result (2026-09-04T03:56Z to 04:0xZ, atmbench, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 focused GO): at 3a9aa54d5 uds f8 requested equals accepted equals durable equals 1000000 with p50 6183.73 (evidence 20260904-035647.863931-local-uds-f8.json); tcp f8 1000000 exact with p50 6324.26 (evidence 20260904-040035.831965-local-tcp-f8.json). Conclusive: the pool bound of 64 performs the same as the bound of 8 (f5de13551: 6105.66 and 5523.52), so the short-N r5 numbers were run-length skew and the control-path pool bound is not the lever for the gap to the floors. Both lanes still miss the floors; r6 measurement-first bisect proceeds as dispatched. Fix round 6 bisect COMPLETE (2026-09-04T04:05Z to 04:55Z, atmbench uds f8, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 BISECT GO; sustained = 1000000 requests, short = duration-bounded): 93aff0f99 sustained exact p50 22840.37 PASS (last all-lanes-PASS revision, campaign 20260826T204324Z); f99c85656 sustained exact 22603.69 PASS (last first-parent commit before the Phase AQ integration merge); ff7b15f44 short exact 19674.57; 7a9097dbb short exact 19696.78; d9e99b789 short exact 19711.76; 334e5ca89 short exact but 1613.11 FAIL; a3c935639 1624.04; dd6a81196 1564.51; a9a3d9ae, 1f5666fa and ed6af62f5 unmeasurable (admission loss, pre fix round 4); 9ed5b7dd1 sustained exact 10477.07 FAIL. Culprit: merge 334e5ca89 (AQ2 queue-graft, PR 1051), source commit 1c74392a8 (AQ1.7 graft endpoint consumer cutover), which made delivery_policy resolve_recipient_snapshot take runtime.graft_receiver_lease, a blocking control-path SQLite borrow (service_runtime.rs to graft_receiver_endpoint_store lookup via shared_db with_connection) on every local write, executed inline on a Tokio worker. Four independent read-only code passes over the four merges agree and rule out 7a9097dbb, d9e99b789 and a3c935639. Lane asymmetry explained: only the daemon-assembled runtime installs the endpoint store, so the direct sqlite lane short-circuits to Ok(None) while uds, tcp and tcp-tls pay the borrow. The writer batch window (writer/mod.rs BATCH_TIME_BUDGET 1ms, unchanged since the baseline) multiplies the resulting in-flight cap into the observed ceiling. Note the focused sustained run reads higher than the official campaign on the same code (10477 versus 6105 at 9ed5b7dd1), so closure proof must be the official benchmark run. Approved fix plan for fix round 6: daemon-owned in-memory graft endpoint snapshot cache at the runtime/store boundary invalidated on registration, deregistration and expiry; no SQLite borrow on the local write hot path; control-path pool bound reverted to 8; regression test that a local write performs no control-path borrow per message with endpoint lifecycle correctness preserved. Fix round 6 pushed as 39327974c (cache graft receiver leases off write path: service_runtime.rs lease snapshot cache with 1 second TTL and invalidation on register, refresh, unregister and mark-unreachable; control-path bound back to 8 derived from the descriptor budget; regression tests; just lint and just test exit 0). Focused proof at 39327974c (2026-09-04T05:0xZ, atmbench, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 focused GO, matched 1000000 sustained per lane): uds f8 exact p50 10921.58 (r5 6183.73, floor 18000); tcp f8 exact p50 8959.97 (r5 6324.26, floor 17000). Material improvement, floors still failed, record stays open and blocking. The focused number at 9ed5b7dd1 before r6 was 10477.07, so on the focused measurement the cache moved uds by about 4 percent while matched-official r5 to r6 cannot yet be compared; the lease borrow is confirmed but not the dominant cost. Fix round 7 (dispatched 2026-09-04T05:07Z, same branch, measure before fixing): scratch-build discriminator that hard-bypasses the lease resolution in resolve_recipient_snapshot on focused uds f8 (a jump toward the d9e99b789 level of about 19700 means the cache is not hit in the real run, a flat result means the remaining cost is elsewhere on the write path); scratch-build instrumentation counting control-path borrows, spawn_blocking calls and writer batch sizes per 1000000 writes to confirm or kill the 833 times mean batch size hypothesis; code diff of the daemon write path d9e99b789..334e5ca89 for other per-write synchronous work added by the AQ2 merge. Closure proof remains the official benchmark run. Fix round 7 result (2026-09-04T05:1xZ to 05:4xZ): scratch variant 1 (lease resolution hard-bypassed) gave uds f8 sustained p50 10812.97 versus the cached 10921.58, proving the r6 cache effective and the residual cost elsewhere. A read-only code pass over the HEAD write path found that the bare-CLI queue-pull received hook (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/received_hook_selector.rs PullPendingReceivedHook, introduced by 2517d84f6 AQ2.5, after the bisected merge and therefore invisible to the r6 bisect) called clear_queue_marker_after_handoff on every message with no kind guard, unlike the graft emitter, costing one spawn_blocking, a global mutex, a control-path checkout and a second SQLite write transaction (pending_nudge_store clear_pending with_transaction on mail_message_states) per local Immediate write, contending with the batched mailbox writer for the WAL lock, for a marker Immediate writes never set. Scratch variant D (guard the clear with kind equals NudgeKind::Queue) on atmbench under fenix@rand-m5 GO: uds f8 sustained requested equals accepted equals durable equals 1000000, p50 24054.79, above the 18000 floor and above the pre-AQ2 level; selected as the fix. Production commit 40b00b236 (fix(readiness): skip marker work for immediate bare-cli writes): Queue-only marker clear; end-to-end regression test that a local Immediate bare-CLI write performs zero pending control-path borrows and zero extra marker transactions; QA-6 ATM-QA-002 addressed by moving the durable lookup outside the lease map lock with per-key coalescing; QA-6 ATM-QA-003 tautological test removed; just fmt, lint (35) and test exit 0. The writer idle spin candidate is tracked separately as RRG-WRITER-IDLE-SPIN-001 (deferred). Still open: closure requires the official step-1 campaign on the re-cut tag meeting all three network-lane floors with exact admission. OFFICIAL CLOSURE EVIDENCE (v15): official step-1 campaign 20260904T054952Z-m5-atmbench on atmbench@rand-m5.local, prerelease/v1.4.12 candidate 4f1202bf2 (evidence-branch source revision 46d34a933, evidence commit ab948cde5 on evidence/readiness-1.4.12-atmbench), started 2026-09-04T05:49:52Z completed 05:51:24Z, status PASS. Lanes (p50 msg/s vs floor, requested/admitted/durable): sqlite 49605.64 vs 35000 (953000/953000/953000); uds 21832.42 vs 18000 (434000/434000/434000); tcp 18671.16 vs 17000 (369000/369000/369000); tcp-tls 16361.64 vs 13500 (325000/325000/325000). Admission and durability exact on every lane, incomplete_reason null everywhere, durability_after_restart passed on all four. The smoke thorough stage also passed on the same host and commit (site/reports/smoke/macos/rand-m5.local/20260904T054723465480Z-pid52930-smoke-thorough). This is the official-run proof the record required; the finding is ready for quality-mgr closure. Not part of this finding: the read family (benchmark-read) has not yet run on 1.4.12 because the atmbench account-local daemon service is not registered, tracked separately." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
